  "id": "COMPOUND:24597 - PROTEIN:3990",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Shengmating and the Inner centromere protein through a series of molecular interactions. Shengmating is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Stilbostemin B 3'-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and Lehualide A, both of which are implicated in targeting the PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2. This kinase is subsequently shown to have a target of the Inner centromere protein, indicating a pathway where Shengmating may influence the activity of CDC2L2, which in turn affects the Inner centromere protein. The scores from the paths are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological link, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible regulatory role of Shengmating in the functional regulation of the Inner centromere protein through the CDC2L2 pathway.",
